 ],
 "description": "### Summary\n\nAn attacker sending an absolute-form request can spoof the scheme used.\n\n### Impact\n\nIf user code depends on the `Request.scheme` attribute for anything security related, an attacker may be able to circumvent this logic, tricking the application into thinking a connection is encrypted when it is not, or vice versa.\n\n### Workaround\n\nA WAF rule to reject absolute-form requests (legitimate requests should only use this form for proxies).",
